# Line endings and binary files for GUI.Forms.
#
# Every text file is stored with LF and checked out with LF on every host,
# whatever core.autocrlf says. A Windows checkout then has the same bytes as a
# Linux or macOS one, so compiler-cache keys, file hashes and fixture
# comparisons agree across hosts, and a shell that would stage CRLF cannot
# commit it. Git decides what is text (text=auto); the lists below say it
# explicitly where a guess would be wrong or costly.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never converted, never diffed or merged as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.ogg binary

# Byte-exact fixtures and corpora: their bytes are the test input or are named
# by a recorded hash, so git never converts them, on checkout or on commit.
# A corpus file added with CRLF keeps it.
fuzz/corpus/** -text
stx_rtf2md/tests/corpus/** -text
tools/font_metrics_differential/corpus/** -text
# The license bytes that tests/fonts/*/PROVENANCE.md hashes.
tests/fonts/*/OFL.txt -text

# Generated files: rewritten by the tools named in their first lines and
# checked by those tools' --check modes. Hidden from review diffs by default.
docs/api/** linguist-generated
docs/controls/generated/** linguist-generated
demo/gallery_catalog.inc linguist-generated
manifests/control-schema.json linguist-generated
generated/** linguist-generated
src/core/text/unicode/unicode_grapheme_data.hpp linguist-generated
tests/unicode_grapheme_break_cases.hpp linguist-generated
tests/doc_examples_compile_only.cpp linguist-generated
tests/doc_examples_tests.cpp linguist-generated
